    "summary": "Man&#039;s gown (tobe, boubou); made of narrow strips of indigo-dyed, white, natural and brown-dyed cotton, machine stitched together. Wide sleeves with cloth cut at right angles ot the body of the gown; irregular neck opening with triangular pocket on left proper chest. Sleeves and hem machine stitched. Reinforced on inside with white cotton cloth around neck and front opening. Strip of white cotton cloth stitched to front of gown at one side of opening and around neck.",
